.page alias 1 define or show command aliases
.alias unalias

# SYNOPSIS
*alias* [_NAME_[=_VALUE_]]...
*unalias* _NAME_...

# DESCRIPTION
`alias` is a gapsh builtin. `alias NAME=VALUE` makes the word _NAME_ stand for _VALUE_ when it is the first word of a command; the remaining words of the command are appended. Without arguments all aliases are listed; with just a name that alias is shown. `unalias` removes aliases.

The login profile defines `ll`, `la`, `l`, `..`, `grep`, `cls`, `shutdown`, `exorcise`, `spellcards` and `netherworld` (see profile(5)).

# EXAMPLES
    alias ll='ls -l'
    alias
    unalias ll

# SEE ALSO
type(1), command(1), profile(5)
